    "text": "A thin uniform annular disc of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>,&nbsp;has an outer radius of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi></math> and an inner radius of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;as shown in the figure. The work required to take a unit mass from point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;on its axis to infinity is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-05-24_at_8.23.38_PM_1.jpeg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 148px;\" />",
